course: dictionary
lesson: 13226
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and gannet is one of them. The words around it are the context, and they tell you which meaning the writer wants. «A gannet dived into the sea and came up with a fish.» The clues are sea and fish, so a gannet here is a bird.
explain: «You greedy gannet, you have eaten all the cake!» Now the clues are greedy and eaten all the cake. Here a gannet is a person who eats too much, very fast. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning and reading the sentence again. If it sounds silly, try the other meaning. The dictionary lists both meanings, so you can always look back to confirm.
fact: A gannet is a large white seabird with black wing tips and a yellowish head.
fact: Gannets dive from high up in the air into the sea to catch fish.
fact: Gannets nest together in big groups called colonies, often on cliffs and islands.
fact: In informal British talk, a gannet is a greedy person who eats a lot, very fast.
fact: Gannet is a noun: one gannet, and more than one gannets.
exercise: «A gannet dived from high above the waves.» What is a gannet in this sentence? | *A large white seabird that dives for fish | A fish with a long, sharp tail | A kind of cloud | A small boat on the sea
exercise: «You greedy gannet, you have eaten all the cake!» What does gannet mean here? | A seabird with black wing tips | A big cake with white icing | *A greedy person who eats a lot, very fast
exercise: «The gannets nested in a huge colony on the cliff.» Find the word that means a large group of birds living together. | cliff | nested | *colony | huge
test: «Dad said, "Stop being such a gannet and share the sweets!"» What does gannet mean here? | A type of fishing boat | A tall rock in the sea | A seabird with black wing tips | *A greedy person who eats too much
test: Which sentence uses gannet to mean a seabird? | Pass the gannet the biscuits, please. | *The gannet hit the water like a white spear. | You greedy gannet, stop eating!
exam: Ella says a gannet is a bird that eats fish, and her brother says it means a greedy person. Who is right? | *Both are right, because gannet has two meanings and the clues in each sentence show which one | Only Ella, because gannet can only mean a bird | Only her brother, because gannets never eat fish | Neither, because gannet has no meaning in the dictionary
